--- Page 21 ---
4/25/2025 Ms. Neeshu Chaudhary, CSE dept 21                      Protected access modifier 
▪Protected  access modifier plays a key role in inheritance. 
▪Protected  members of the class can be accessed within the class 
and from derived class but cannot be accessed from any other 
class or program. 
▪It works like public for derived class and private for other class. 

--- Page 22 ---
4/25/2025 Ms. Neeshu Chaudhary, CSE dept 22
class ABC {   
public :  
   void setProtMemb( int i){ 
     m_protMemb = i; }   
   void Display(){  
     cout<<m_protMemb<<endl;}   
protected :  
   int  m_protMemb;   
   void Protfunc(){  
     cout<< "\nAccess allowed\n" ;}  };  
class XYZ : public  ABC{   
public :  
   void useProtfunc(){  
     Protfunc(); }   
}; 
int main() {   
   ABC a; XYZ x;  
   a.m_protMemb;  
   a.setProtMemb(0);  
   a.Display();   
   a.Protfunc();  
   x.setProtMemb(5);   
   x.Display();   
   x.useProtfunc();}  

